## Live session tracking

`src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:38` — a module-private `Map<string, PtyRecord>`:
```ts
const ptys = new Map<string, PtyRecord>();
```
Keyed by session id (task id, or `shell:<taskId>[:N]` for terminal-drawer shells, or feature-scoped ids for TUI side-cars). Each `PtyRecord` (`ptys.ts:21-36`) holds the `IPty` handle (`proc`), `cwd`, owning `WebContents`, `kind` (`'agent'|'shell'|'tui'|'service'`), `taskId`/`featureId`, and a headless `TerminalMirror` used to replay output on renderer reattach.

## Resize

`src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:695-705`:
```ts
export function resizePty(id: string, cols: number, rows: number): void {
  const record = ptys.get(id);
  if (record) {
    record.mirror?.resize(cols, rows);
    try {
      record.proc.resize(cols, rows);
    } catch {
      // EBADF can happen during transitions
    }
  }
}
```
It resizes the headless mirror (so a reattaching xterm gets the right dimensions) and the real PTY, guarding `proc.resize()` in a try/catch since an EBADF can occur mid-transition (e.g. process already exiting). This is invoked over IPC from the renderer's `TerminalSessionManager` (`src/renderer/terminal/TerminalSessionManager.ts`) via the exposed `electron-api` (`src/types/electron-api/pty.ts`), which forwards renderer-side xterm.js resize events into this function through `dbIpc`/pty IPC handlers in `src/main/main.ts`.

## Shutdown, with timeout

Graceful two-phase kill, `src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:708` and `727-763`:
```ts
const GRACEFUL_KILL_TIMEOUT_MS = 3000;

function gracefulKillProc(proc: KillableProc, timeoutMs = GRACEFUL_KILL_TIMEOUT_MS): Promise<void> {
  return new Promise<void>((resolve) => {
    ...
    try {
      disposable = proc.onExit(() => finish());
    } catch { ... }
    timer = setTimeout(() => {
      try { proc.kill('SIGKILL'); } catch { ... }
      finish();
    }, timeoutMs);
    try {
      proc.kill('SIGTERM');
    } catch {
      finish();
    }
  });
}
```
It sends `SIGTERM` first (comment at `ptyManager.ts:715-718` explains this deliberately avoids node-pty's default `kill()`, which sends `SIGHUP` — untrapped by Claude Code, so the in-memory session tail was lost). If the process hasn't exited within **3000ms** (`GRACEFUL_KILL_TIMEOUT_MS`), it escalates to `SIGKILL`. The promise resolves once the process actually exits or the timeout fires.

This is wrapped by `killPtyInternal` (`ptyManager.ts:777-782`), exposed as fire-and-forget `killPty` (`789-791`) and awaitable `killPtyAwait` (`799-801`), and used in bulk by `killAll` (`808-818`, on app quit — all children killed in parallel so total wait is ~one grace window) and `killByOwner` (`825-832`, on window close).

## Spawn environment (anything special)

Built in `buildDirectEnv` at `src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:231-340`, used at the actual `pty.spawn()` call site (`503-509`). Notable non-default behavior:

- **Minimal-by-default env** (`233-235`): unless `syncShellEnv` is on, it does *not* inherit `process.env` wholesale — it starts from `{}` and builds up explicitly, for "fast, predictable spawns."
- `TERM_PROGRAM: 'dash'`, forced `TERM=xterm-256color`/`COLORTERM=truecolor` on non-Windows (`246`, `279-280`).
- `COLORFGBG` synthesized from the app's dark/light theme (`251`) so CLI apps in the PTY can detect the terminal background.
- PATH is merged with a Dash-managed `rtk` binary dir if present (`239-242`).
- Explicit auth passthrough allowlist (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `GH_TOKEN`, proxy vars, etc., `286-303`) only when not doing full env inheritance.
- User-configured env vars merged in but filtered against a `RESERVED_ENV_KEYS` set (`127-138`, `307-311`) — can't override `PATH`, `HOME`, `TERM`, `DASH_HOOK_PORT`, etc.
- Per-task port env vars injected from `WorkspacePortsRuntime.getEnvForWorktree(cwd)` (`320-324`) so commands run inside the PTY see the same ports as the UI's ports panel.
- `CLAUDE_CODE_NO_FLICKER=1` (`327`) to disable Claude Code's own viewport scrolling since Dash renders its own terminal viewport.
- `DASH_HOOK_PORT` set last (`335-337`) pointing at the live `HookServer`, so hook scripts written to `.claude/settings.local.json` know where to `curl` back to.
- Windows gets a separate branch pulling in `SystemRoot`/`APPDATA`/`COMSPEC` etc. (`254-277`), since those are required for DNS/credential-store/Node to function at all.

The plain shell path (`startPty`, `563-623`) is different: it inherits full `process.env`, strips Electron artifacts (`ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE`, `ELECTRON_NO_ATTACH_CONSOLE`, `593-594`), forces `Apple_Terminal` on macOS for OSC 7 cwd reporting (`599`), and for zsh sets `ZDOTDIR` to a Dash-managed shell config directory (`604`) to inject a custom prompt — and spawns with `-i` (interactive, not login) intentionally, since login-shell startup files add ~0.5s and PATH is already fixed up at app boot (`587`).
